$\angle AXB=38^\circ$ (alternate angles on parallel north lines).
$$\begin{align*}
\angle ABX &= 360^\circ-325^\circ=35^\circ \\
\angle BAX &= 180^\circ-38^\circ-35^\circ=107^\circ \\
\frac{BA}{\sin38^\circ} &= \frac{BX}{\sin107^\circ} \\
BA &= \frac{(5.8\tan72^\circ)\sin38^\circ}{\sin107^\circ}
\end{align*}$$
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{AX}{\sin35^\circ} &= \frac{BX}{\sin107^\circ} \\
AX &= \frac{(5.8\tan72^\circ)\sin35^\circ}{\sin107^\circ} \\
BA+AX &= \frac{5.8\tan72^\circ(\sin38^\circ+\sin35^\circ)}{\sin107^\circ} \\
BA+AX &\approx22.2\text{ km}
\end{align*}$$
